{"packet_id":"D032-01","doc_id":"D032","jurisdiction":"Hoboken, NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Hoboken rent leveling and stabilization controls","requirement":"Rents are controlled at the base rent received as of October 1, 1985; a landlord may not charge more than the chapter allows and must give 30 days' written notice explaining any increase.","key_value":"Base rent as of October 1, 1985 + allowable increases","coverage_conditions":"All dwelling units, except newly constructed dwellings on first rental, industrial, nonresidential/commercial, school or government housing, buildings vacant since January 1, 1984, and multiple dwellings built after June 25, 1987.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1987-06-25","basis":"construction","conditional":true},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"school, college or similar institution","unit_limit":null},{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"state or federal government agency","unit_limit":null},{"type":"other","text":"newly constructed dwelling on its first rental, registered before first rental"},{"type":"other","text":"building completely vacant on or before and since January 1, 1984"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["This chapter shall apply to all dwelling units as defined in § 155-1 above, except that the following shall be exempt:","Housing provided for students by a school, college or similar institution which owns or controls that housing.","In accordance with N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.1 et seq., the provisions of this chapter shall not apply to multiple dwellings, as defined in the statute, constructed after June 25, 1987, for a period not to exceed the period of amortization of any initial mortgage loan obtained for the multiple dwelling or for 30 years following completion of construction, whichever is less."]},"exemptions":"Motels and hotels; newly constructed dwellings on first rental; industrial; nonresidential and commercial property; school or government housing; buildings vacant since January 1, 1984; multiple dwellings constructed after June 25, 1987.","penalty":"Excess rent increases are void and excess rents must be refunded or credited to the tenant; refunds/credits are barred after two years.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"Hoboken, N.J., Code § 155-4","quoted_span":"All rents for rental of housing space and services in dwellings to which this act is applicable are hereby controlled at the base rent level received by the landlord as of October 1, 1985, and no rental increases shall be hereinafter demanded, paid or accepted, except as provided in this chapter.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.9,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D032-01","doc_id":"D032","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New-construction exemption from local rent control (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.1)","requirement":"Local rent control does not apply to multiple dwellings constructed after June 25, 1987, for up to 30 years or the initial mortgage loan amortization period, whichever is less, if the landlord met the statute's notice requirements.","key_value":"30 years or mortgage amortization, whichever is less","coverage_conditions":"Multiple dwellings constructed after June 25, 1987; exemption requires notice to the Construction Code Official at least 30 days before the certificate of occupancy and lease notice to tenants.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built","role":"exempt","op":"after","date":"1987-06-25","basis":"construction","conditional":true}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["In accordance with N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.1 et seq., the provisions of this chapter shall not apply to multiple dwellings, as defined in the statute, constructed after June 25, 1987, for a period not to exceed the period of amortization of any initial mortgage loan obtained for the multiple dwelling or for 30 years following completion of construction, whichever is less."]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.1","quoted_span":"In accordance with N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.1 et seq., the provisions of this chapter shall not apply to multiple dwellings, as defined in the statute, constructed after June 25, 1987, for a period not to exceed the period of amortization of any initial mortgage loan obtained for the multiple dwelling or for 30 years following completion of construction, whichever is less.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D032-01","n_rules":2,"note":null}

